Description: panfrost: mark a BO shared when its KMS handle is exported
 The caller of resource_get_handle() with WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_KMS can turn the
 GEM handle into a dma-buf itself (drmPrimeHandleToFD(), as Chromium does).
 Mark the BO as shared so that it does not go back to the BO cache and get
 recycled while another user still holds it. freedreno does the same.
Author: pocket-debs
Forwarded: no
License: MIT (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-19
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -443,6 +443,11 @@ panfrost_resource_get_handle(struct pipe
    if (handle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_KMS && dev->ro) {
       return renderonly_get_handle(scanout, handle);
    } else if (handle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_KMS) {
+      /* The caller can turn the GEM handle into a dma-buf itself
+       * (drmPrimeHandleToFD()), so the BO must not go back to the BO cache
+       * and be recycled while someone else still uses it.
+       */
+      rsrc->bo->flags |= PAN_BO_SHARED;
       handle->handle = panfrost_bo_handle(rsrc->bo);
    } else if (handle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_FD) {
       int fd = panfrost_bo_export(rsrc->bo);
